mbp16-1: smooth t2fanrd ramp-up (upstream GnomedDev/T2FanRD 48baf96, GPL-3.0-or-later)

Same revision as Omarchy's t2fanrd r16.48baf96 package. Curve, min and max
speeds unchanged.

1. After each 1 s idle sleep, upstream back-fills the 50-slot mean with 10
   copies of the NEW reading. A launch moves the mean by a fifth of the step
   at once, so the fans jump, then reach max in ~3 s. Hold the PREVIOUS
   reading for the slept second instead (window stays ~5 s).
2. Optional per-fan `ramp_up_s` in /etc/t2fand.conf: a rise covers at most
   the full min-to-max range in that many seconds. Falls are immediate (the
   5 s mean already smooths them). Absent or 0 = upstream behaviour. Stock
   t2fanrd ignores the key.

Applied by `mbp16-1 apply fans` with `git apply` on a pinned checkout.

